<div class="col-xs-12 tmpl-container informazioni" style="padding: 0;">
<div class="pages-basic-info" style="clear: both; overflow: hidden;"><span class="am am-bookmark set-color" style="font-size: 50px; color: #a91a2d; position: absolute; left: 31px; top: -15px;"></span>
<div class="col-xs-12 col-sm-6 col-md-6 " style="margin-top: 10px; padding-left: 0px; padding-right: 0px;">
<p class="basic-info-title" style="color: #a91a2d;">Information</p>
<div class="m-t-10 m-b-10 nop locked-text"><span class="am am-pin" style="margin-right: 10px;"></span> <a href="https://goo.gl/maps/Jg4rx23jZy4ZPoip9" target="_blank" style="font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; color: #000;" title="Vedi su Maps"> <span style="text-decoration: underline;" class="m-r-5"> <span><strong><span class="street-address">L.go Castello, 1</span>, <span class="postal-code">44121</span> <span class="locality">Ferrara</span> <span class="region">FE</span>, <span class="country-name">Italy</span></strong></span> <span class="am am-open-in-new"> </span> </span></a></div>
<div class="m-t-10 m-b-10 nop">
<div class="info-accordion"><span class="am am-calendar-check" style="margin-right: 10px;"></span> <span class="accordion" onclick="$(this).next().next().slideToggle(); $(this).next().toggleClass('am-chevron-up')"><strong>Opening time</strong></span> <span class="accrodion-chevron am am-chevron-down" style="margin-left: 10px;" onclick="$(this).next().slideToggle();"></span>
<div class="accordion-content" style="display: none;">
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Wednesday to Monday</strong>, 10 am to 6 pm<br />Ticket office closes at 5:15 pm</p>
<p class="p1"><i>Aforementioned are standard museum hours. For all updates regarding any changes in hours and opening days click&nbsp;<a href="https://www.ferrarainfo.com/en/where-to-go/city-and-territory/ferrara/museums-and-monuments-of-ferrara" target="_blank"><strong><span style="background-color: #800000; color: #ffffff;"> &nbsp;HERE&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></strong></a></i></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="m-t-10 m-b-10 nop">
<div class="info-accordion"><span class="am am-ticket-star" style="margin-right: 10px;"></span> <span class="accordion" onclick="$(this).next().next().slideToggle(); $(this).next().toggleClass('am-chevron-up')"><strong>Tickets and accessibility</strong></span> <span class="accrodion-chevron am am-chevron-down" style="margin-left: 10px;" onclick="$(this).next().slideToggle();"></span>
<div class="accordion-content" style="display: none;">
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #800000;"><strong>Tickets<br /></strong></span><strong>Full ticket:</strong> &euro; 12<br /><br /><strong>Reduced ticket:</strong> &euro; 10&nbsp;<br />over 65-years-old<br />members of groups of at least 15 people<br />university students with a university course registration card<br />holders of a full or reduced ticket of <a href="https://www.ferraraarte.it/" target="_self">Ferrara Arte</a> exhibitions<br />Coop Alleanza members<br />FAI members</p>
<p><strong>Reduced ticket:</strong> &euro; 5<br />Middle and high school groups<br />Minors between 11 and 18 years old</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Family admission:</strong> for every paying adult, one minor gets in free<br /><br />For access to Torre dei Leoni (panoramic view): &euro; 2 &ndash; free for <a href="https://www.ferraraterraeacqua.it/en/myfecard/what-is-myfe-card?set_language=en" target="_self">MyFE Card</a> holders<br /><br /><strong>Free admission:<br /></strong><a href="https://www.ferraraterraeacqua.it/en/myfecard/what-is-myfe-card?set_language=en" target="_self">MyFE</a> cardholders<br />under 11 years old<br />one minor for each paying adult<br />tour guides, tour leaders, environmental hiking guides, interpreters and teachers in the exercise of their professional activity<br />disabled persons and their companions<br />card-carrying journalists and publicists<br />visitors accessing the castle on their birthday or, if the castle is closed on their birthday, on the first available open day<br />students enrolled in their first year at the University of Ferrara with a student ID.<br /><br /></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #800000;"><strong>Accessibility<br /></strong></span>The entire Castle is accessible to people with disabilities and reduced mobility, except for the dungeon rooms.<br />Disabled people in wheelchairs can visit the entire castle by ascending to the second floor using the elevator in the southwest tower of San Paolo.<br />For more detailed information on accessibility visit the ticket office.&nbsp; Assistance points are available along the way.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-xs-12 col-sm-6 map-container">
<div class="">
<div class="real_google_map_place"><input type="hidden" id="place-id-indirizzo" name="Pagine[indirizzo]" value="ChIJOTirVxNOfkcR_yOjTDpOhsc"><input type="text" id="pac-input-indirizzo" class="controls hidden" name="tmp-pac-input_indirizzo" value=""><div id="map-loader-indirizzo" class="map-loader">Loading map<br /><div id="progress-indirizzo" class="progress"><div class="progress-bar progress-bar-striped active" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="100" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" style="width:100%"></div></div></div><div id="map-indirizzo" class="map" data-attribute="indirizzo"></div></div>
<div class="fake_google_map_place hide locked"><img style="width: 100%;" src="/assets/1ca9e6b31b9cf974a974088b1c241b39/img/map_place.png" /></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<h2 style="text-align: left;"><span style="color: #800000;">The Este Castle of Ferrara</span></h2>
<p>The Castello Estense amazes those who arrive in Ferrara with its grandeur. <strong>An almost unexpected fortress, it stands out in the city centre</strong>, now as in the past. Surrounded by a moat and drawbridges, it always attracts the curiosity of visitors.</p>
<p>Kissed by the summer sun or bathed in an eerie blanket of fog, it is the true <strong>symbol of the city</strong>. A must-see destination for visitors, this fortress still retains its charm and magnificence intact to this day &ndash; we are sure it will wow you!&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><img src="https://www.inferrara.it/attachments/file/view?hash=92e93e32744e436d0a1f5bd881a47c8ed395f611b59a5d767dae1a7ed1592c31&amp;canCache=1" alt="" width="1200" height="1200" /></p>
<h2 style="text-align: left;"><span style="color: #800000;">The Este Castle - Historical notes</span></h2>
<p>Ferrara, September 3, 1385. Violent popular riots shake the city while the people of Ferrara are oppressed by taxes. Marquis Niccol&ograve; d'Este, intimidated by his citizens, decides to have a fortress built connected to his residence, today's Municipal Palace. This is how, on September 29 of the same year, the first foundation stone of Ferrara's Castello Estense was laid.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Named after Saint Michael and built by Bartolino da Novara, the Castello Estense was embellished over the centuries to become the magnificent residence of the Este court. Altanas above the towers, marble balconies, a courtyard of honour with 16th-century lines and sumptuous frescoed apartments enriched the structure over the years.&nbsp;</p>
<p>The imposing four towers, set at the four corners of the Castle of San Michele, still tower over the city, an indelible symbol of the grandeur and magnificence of the Este family. It is impossible not to take a photograph of the Torre dei Leoni, an exceptional vantage point from which to admire the historical centre and beyond.</p>
<p><img src="https://www.inferrara.it/static/de/5a/08/deb5ab086decb30d9161eff96d570cd7ec80646e559a5bce31a8ace4c31752c7.jpg" alt="Castello estense di Ferrara" width="1200" height="799" /></p>
<h2 style="text-align: left;"><span style="color: #800000;">The Este Castle - </span><span style="color: #800000;">The visit</span></h2>
<p>Upon entering the marvellous Cortile del Castello Estense, the visitor will find himself immersed in its history and that of the characters who populated it. From the events of the d'Este family to the Unification of Italy, passing through those related to the Papal State.&nbsp;</p>
<p>You will be able to stroll among the splendid orange trees in the panoramic garden of the same name, commissioned by Alfonso I d'Este. Learn the stories of Ugo and Parisina Malatesta, the two lovers made famous by their unfortunate fate. Visit the prisons, including the cramped cell where Giulio d'Este was imprisoned for no less than 53 years.</p>
<p>Marvel at the frescoes adorning the rooms of the so-called Appartamento dello Specchio, built at the behest of Alfonso II d'Este, and the other elegant staterooms.&nbsp;</p>
<h4>An unmissable journey through time and the city's history.&nbsp;</h4>
<div class="mceTemplate row">
<div class="col-xs-12 tmpl-container colonne colonne2" style="padding: 0;">
<div class="row">
<div class="col-xs-12 col-sm-6 col-md-6">
<div>
<p><img src="https://www.inferrara.it/static/a4/23/6b/a4223e6b504cedb8e7300249af33c3f6ccd6bc2c9f6685b1f06dde7f3a50eea3.jpg" alt="Mostra interna Castello Estense di Ferrara" width="1200" height="799" /></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-xs-12 col-sm-6 col-md-6">
<div>
<p><img src="https://www.inferrara.it/static/0f/89/89/0f38988920d7a3ae3cd39ae3f9d7e65eeda5ed75ed8f5f897cdcd79ca3b26540.jpg" alt="Mostra interna Castello estense di Ferrara" width="1200" height="799" /></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<h3>You may not know about...</h3>
<p><strong>THE CASTLE FIRE.</strong> Every December 31, the Estense Castle is the stage for a breathtaking firework display. Tens of thousands of people come to the square to witness what is described as one of the most beautiful New Year's Eve shows in all of Europe.&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>THE TRAGICAL LOVE OF UGO AND PARISINA.</strong> It is one of the most famous, albeit unfortunate, loves of the Este family. The wife of Niccol&ograve; III d'Este, Laura Malatesta, known as Parisina, fell in love with her stepson Ugo whom the marquis had married to the beloved Stella de Tolomei. Discovered, the two lovers were imprisoned and beheaded in the castle dungeon.&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>IN THE HALL OF COATS OF ARMS.</strong> What is the blackened pane on the north wall? Legate Count Filippo Folicardi, implicated in a smuggling trial, was removed from Ferrara in 1856. With him, his coat of arms and his memory, no longer worthy of being part of the hall's decorative scheme.&nbsp;</p>                    </div>
                </div>
            
